SQLite for generated9

Build with the native Plan 9 compiler and libc:

    cd /sys/src/libsqlite3
    mk install
    mk test
    cd /sys/src/cmd/sqlite3
    mk install
    mk test

Compile clients with -p and include <u.h>, <libc.h>, <sqlite3.h>.
The header selects libsqlite3.a. No APE or host compiler is needed.
On amd64, use the rebuilt 6c described in boot/README.md.

See sqlite3(1) for the command and sqlite3(2) for the VFS contract and limits.
Database files require DMEXCL for the connection's lifetime and stable-storage
wstat barriers. Use gefs for persistent storage or ramfs for temporary data.
u9fs rejects DMEXCL; lease-expiring servers such as cwfs are not supported.
The database format is unchanged. Closed databases can be copied to other
systems; import a database onto a suitable server and set chmod +l before use.

mk test uses a private ramfs. To test a persistent server, create an empty
directory there and run:

    cd /sys/src/libsqlite3/test
    mk
    ./6.out /n/fs/sqlite-test

The suite checks SQL and numeric boundaries, bindings, attached databases,
journal modes, vacuum, file I/O, exclusive opens, renamed databases, process
death, and recovery at each VFS xWrite/xSync call in a transaction.
It leaves test.db in the supplied directory.
These are application-crash tests, not a power-loss certification of the server.

Optional numerical comparison against the host's Python SQLite:

    python3 sys/src/libsqlite3/test/compare.py generate usr/glenda/tmp/sqlite-compare

Inside generated9:

    sqlite3 :memory: </tmp/sqlite-compare/numeric.sql >/tmp/sqlite-compare/numeric.out

Then on the host:

    python3 sys/src/libsqlite3/test/compare.py check usr/glenda/tmp/sqlite-compare

Runtime validation: amd64, ramfs and gefs. Sources and licenses: UPSTREAM.
